      "writtenOn": "2018-11-15T20:50:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This should be package private or more ; there is no point having a private accessor that only returns a member.\n\nThe reason the outer class is able to see this is because enclosing classes are defined as being able to access private members, and Java does that by creating a synthetic public accessor. So in this case, you have the outer class calling the synthetic accessor, which calls this accessor, which returns the member. The class is already protected (and private in spirit) so you can cut the middle man.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1569,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 1569,
        "endChar": 15
      },
